# Anchor Billing Workflow — Setup + First Month at Signing, Recurring on 1st/15th

> **Purpose:** Collect setup + first month as a lump at signing, then anchor all future recurring billing to the 1st or 15th of the month — with no proration. Every mechanism below is **confirmed present** in the GHL account (verified field-by-field, not assumed).

---

## The policy this implements

- **At signing:** client pays a lump = **setup fee + first month** (one-time). Card is captured.
- **Recurring:** starts on the next anchor (1st or 15th) *after their prepaid month is used up*, then repeats monthly on that anchor.
- **No proration.** The gap between "prepaid month ends" and "next anchor" is free goodwill — capped at ~2 weeks by using two anchors (1st & 15th) instead of one.
- **Why two anchors:** a couple weeks free is acceptable goodwill; a whole month free (single anchor) is not. Two anchors caps the giveaway.
- **The double-bill trap (critical):** because they prepaid a full month, the recurring must NOT start on the *immediate* next anchor (could be days away → double charge). It must start on the anchor *after* the prepaid ~30 days. The 31-day wait below handles this.

---

## Step 1 — Two products (Payments → Products)

1. **Signup product (one-time)** — name e.g. "Service Signup — Setup + First Month." Type: **One-Time**. Price: **setup fee + one month** (the lump due at signing). This captures the card and is the workflow trigger.
2. **Recurring product (monthly)** — name e.g. "Monthly Membership — Ongoing." Type: **Recurring / Monthly**. Price: full monthly amount. This is what the recurring invoice bills from the anchor onward.

*(Per tier, you'd have a signup product and a recurring product. The signup product's price = that tier's setup + that tier's monthly.)*

---

## Step 2 — The workflow

**Trigger:** Order/Signup product purchased (the one-time signup product).

**Action 1 — Wait "For a set period of time": 31 days.**
Burns through the prepaid month so the recurring can't double-bill. Use 31 (not 30) to cover long months and guarantee the prepaid month is fully consumed.

**Action 2 — If/Else (condition: "Current Day of month"):**
- **Branch A:** Current Day of month **is on or before 14** → go to Action 3A.
- **None / else** (days 15–31): → go to Action 3B.

*(Note: this evaluates the day of month AFTER the 31-day wait, not the signup day — so it routes to the nearest anchor from that point.)*

**Action 3A — Wait "Until a recurring window opens":** Frequency **Monthly**, **Day 15**, all 12 months.
**Action 3B — Wait "Until a recurring window opens":** Frequency **Monthly**, **Day 1**, all 12 months.

*(A single recurring-window wait only targets ONE day of the month — that's why the branch splits into two waits.)*

**Action 4 — Both branches converge → "Send recurring invoice" (Payments action):**
- **From User:** (McKay)
- **Invoice Template:** the recurring product
- **Payment Mode (Live):** ON
- **Start Date:** **Action Date** (recurring begins when the contact reaches this step — i.e., right after the anchor wait releases them, so it anchors to that day)
- **End:** **Never** (perpetual — never bill-once-and-stop)
- **How Often:** Monthly, Every **1**
- **Enable Autopayment:** **ON** — "card used to pay first invoice will be auto-deducted for subsequent invoices" (uses the signing card automatically)
- **Channel:** Email & Text

---

## Flow, end to end

Client signs → pays setup + first month lump (card captured) → 31-day wait burns the prepaid month → branch checks day of month → waits until the next 1st or 15th → recurring invoice starts there, auto-charging the saved card, monthly, forever.

**Example (signs up Oct 5):** pays lump Oct 5 → 31-day wait to ~Nov 5 → day is 5 (≤14) → wait until Nov 15 → recurring starts Nov 15, repeats the 15th monthly. Free goodwill days: ~Nov 5–15.

